{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Introduce minimum wage standards & workplace safety protections for care workers",
        "additional_details": "Care workers have been killed doing their jobs. A survey found that 52% of care workers surveyed had been physically assaulted at work. We can be sent alone into homes without backup where we may face risks to our safety. We believe the cost of living is putting financial pressure on care workers and some of us are not paid separately for travel between calls. We believe care workers need better pay and stronger workplace safety protections.",
        "background": "We want professional minimum wages and enforceable workplace safety protections for all community and domiciliary carers. We want a legally binding Care Workers' Bill of Rights to mandate minimum pay standards and enforceable workplace safety protections for all community and domiciliary carers.",
